              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "EmeeDee"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Found this while searching for a heart healthy dressing for pasta. Small changes I made: I used the called for 1/4 cup each of vinegar &amp; oil, but then added enough to make 3/4 cup total. Used Garlic Pepper instead of garlic (to taste). 2 tsp of lemon juice instead of zest. 1 tsp of brown mustard was more than enough. Added a little bit of basil &amp; some garlic salt. Poured over Penne pasta. Yum!",
            "datePublished": "2011-04-12T15:11:45.150Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "dozy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made this for salad to go w the lime garlic chicken (by Cristina r. De c. On this site. ) amaaaaazing! Love it. Used red wine vinegar instead of white (was all I had) and ReaLemon juice. Made up my own proportions (didn't measure anything- just guesstimate ) I've made it a few times and it's always great!!",
            "datePublished": "2014-05-06T14:33:07.880Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "crazycatlady - CCL"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Loved it! I used a \"pink\" packet rather than sugar &amp; used a teaspoon of fresh lemon juice. My oil was garlic infused, so I omitted the minced garlic, but did add some black pepper. The family had this over (mixed) green salad &amp; I had it over cucumbers. YUM! Thanks for sharing the recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2012-01-13T15:32:54.450Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
